  "acceptance_use": "ac_10_performance_evidence",
  "blocked_change": "The pinned external TVM NVSHMEM runtime must separate the distributed PE/rank from the physical CUDA device ordinal. Modifying that source, monkey-patching it, or restoring CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES masking is outside the authorized implementation boundary.",
  "call_site_alternative_audit": {
    "conclusion": "No existing full-device-init API in the pinned runtime can be called from this repository with separate PE rank and physical CUDA ordinal.",
    "direct_nvshmem_full_init": "nvshmemx_init_attr is a header-inline function that calls nvshmemi_init_thread. The installed shared library marks nvshmemi_init_thread LOCAL, so it is not available through dlsym/ctypes; nvshmemx_hostlib_init_attr is exported but is not the complete device initialization used by the TVM runtime.",
    "disco_default_device": "Setting a Disco worker default_device cannot help because InitNVSHMEM calls cudaSetDevice(worker_id) before consulting default_device and later requires default_device to equal mype_node.",
    "registered_tvm_functions": "The pinned TVM runtime registers only init_nvshmem_uid, init_nvshmem, and init_nvshmem_wrapper for this lifecycle; both full-init entry points call the same rank-coupled implementation.",
    "worker_id_start": "worker_id_start cannot carry a physical device ordinal because the same value is passed to nvshmemx_set_attr_uniqueid_args as myrank; for one rank, physical index 2 would produce invalid myrank=2,nranks=1. After initialization, cudaSetDevice(mype_node) would still select 0."
  },
